      "id": 1,
      "text": "Early settler Daniel Dodge Bayley named Garibaldi after Giuseppe Garibaldi, a nineteenth-century Italian military leader and revolutionary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://theoregoncoastguide.com/garibaldi-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Garibaldi began as a fishing village in the late nineteenth century and remains a working harbor town on Tillamook Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitoregon.com/cities/garibaldi-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Oregon Coast Scenic Railroad operates restored vintage steam and diesel locomotives that carry passengers along the bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitoregon.com/cities/garibaldi-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Indigenous Tillamook people lived along the coast and Tillamook Bay for about twelve thousand years in permanent cedar-plank lodges.",
